## Instructions
Review the diff for correctness issues. You have the full file to validate that changes integrate properly. Focus on:
- Logic errors, off-by-one errors, incorrect conditions
- Missing null/error checks
- Incorrect API usage or broken contracts
- Race conditions or concurrency issues
- Missing edge cases
- Breaking changes to existing functionality

## Severity Guidelines
Choose the severity that matches the actual impact:
- **error** — Will cause crashes, data loss, or broken functionality (e.g. null dereference, infinite loop, race condition causing corruption)
- **warning** — Likely to cause bugs in edge cases or under certain conditions (e.g. missing error check, mutable default argument, off-by-one that may not always trigger)
- **suggestion** — Code works but could be improved (e.g. simplifiable logic, missing type hints, verbose patterns)
- **info** — Observations or notes (e.g. TODO comments, minor inconsistencies)

Do NOT mark everything as "error". Reserve "error" for issues that **will** break at runtime.

For each finding, respond with a JSON array:
```json
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "line": 42,
      "end_line": null,
      "severity": "warning",
      "category": "correctness",
      "title": "Short title",
      "description": "Detailed explanation of the issue",
      "suggestion": "corrected code if applicable, or null"
    }
  ]
}
```

If there are no issues, return `{"findings": []}`.
Respond with ONLY the JSON object.
